careful no " - " at end of comment line... "hatch when demographics miss" no dash. The `----` separators like `/* Headline row: ... --------------- */`: sequence of hyphens at end: `--------------` is a run of hyphens NOT spaced (' - ' requires spaces around single hyphen; '-------' contains no 'space hyphen space') ✓ allowed. But careful: `/* ... miss - */`: ends with " - " if I write space hyphen space before */. Avoid: existing file uses `/* Headline panel ---------- */` pattern where hyphens follow text without spaces ✓ e.g. `/* Band cells: glyph, label, count, percent, all on one hue --------------- */` — "hue ---" no space before hyphens ✓. I'll follow exactly: text, space, then hyphens run: "hue ---------------" — space then hyphen run: SPACED_HYPHEN is ' - ' (space-hyphen-space); "hue ---" has no space AFTER hyphen (it's `*/`) ✓ safe. But a run of hyphens ends the comment with `*/`: " -*/"? I write "----- */" → contains " " + "----" + " */": is ' - ' present? substring ' - ' would need space-hyphen-space: in "----- */" after each hyphen comes another hyphen or space then '*'... consider hyphen immediately followed by space: last hyphen then space then '*': ' ' after hyphen, but pattern requires space BEFORE hyphen too: the char before last hyphen is '-' not ' ' → no ' - ' ✓. Safe (existing file proves it).

